{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>And I will set enmity.</b> We have no enmity with the serpent more than with other creeping things, but Scripture alludes in hiddenness, for the body of the cunning serpent was a prepared vessel for punishment, to receive the power that was bound within it — and it was that which caused Ḥavah to sin, and through this death was decreed upon all her seed. And that is the enmity between the serpent and the seed of Ḥavah, and this is the secret of the expression by which the serpent is called <i>seraf</i>, just as the angel is called <i>seraf</i>, as Scripture says (Numbers 21:6): ״את הנחשים השרפים״ — for they were the offspring of the primordial serpent, and understand this. And from this it says, ״הוא ישופך ראש״ and so forth — for a person is able to overcome his impulse and crush it at the outset; and if he does not, ״ואתה תשופנו עקב״ — a hint to you that if a person does not crush this impulse, it will crush him in the end and kill him. And the word עקב alludes to the day of death. And you already know the saying of the Sages, blessed be their memory: he is the Accuser, he is the evil impulse, he is the angel of death."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:09:55.080239686Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}